# KNOWN GAP (`todo/t1067`, the `Mutex`/`RWLock` member) — the SAME capture cell
# as `closure_capture_callable_block_scope_uaf.gg`, with the captured handle a
# `Mutex[int]` instead of a `Callable`. rc 0 printing a garbage integer;
# `AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free` in `gorget_mutex_lock` under
# `--sanitize`.
#
# WHY THIS CELL EXISTS SEPARATELY. The consuming-position carve-out that lets
# both programs build is `TypeRegistry::lacks_materialization_path` —
# `needs_drop && !is_resource_type && !is_refcount_clone_type`. That predicate is
# derived, and what it admits is WIDER than the `Callable` cell alone: `Mutex[T]`
# and `RWLock[T]` are `copy_semantics: Trivial` with `clone_fn = None`
# (single-owner by design, no incref and no deep clone), so they satisfy every
# clause too. An item that named only `Callable` would be presenting a SELECTION
# as a total enumeration; this fixture is the second member.
#
# ⚠ `RWLock[T]` IS THE THIRD MEMBER, NAMED BUT NOT COVERED BY THIS CELL. It
# shares the shape and the mechanism, but not the value of the axis the
# carve-out reads: `Mutex`'s TypeDef is stamped by a builtin path
# (`ensure_mutex_type_def` in `src/ir/lowering/exprs/type_reg.rs`) while
# `RWLock[T]` is a `struct RWLock[T]` template in `lib/std/sync.gg`, so its
# ctor reaches the template-monomorph arm in
# `src/ir/lowering/generics/mod.rs` instead. That arm's own comment records
# this exact metadata once being wrong there and the single-owner handle
# LEAKING on scope exit. A `Mutex` cell cannot see an `RWLock` regression on
# that axis — this is a named omission with a measured reason (Core #12),
# and it earns its own fixture when D7 lands.
#
# ⚠ PRE-EXISTING AND UNCHANGED. Measured at the base commit and after the
# capture-ownership fix: identical garbage value, identical
# `heap-use-after-free` in `gorget_mutex_lock`. The carve-out preserves the
# behaviour rather than creating it — before the fix the whole closure-env
# `StructInit` was skipped by the validator, so this program built for a
# different reason and ran the same way.
#
# ⚠ THE GATE IS D7, NOT THE CAPTURE RULE — same as the `Callable` cell. Clone
# breaches the ratified single-owner carve-out, move breaches it and silently
# consumes under D31 full-strict, and a rejection has no fix-it a user can
# spell until D7's per-variable capture list exists.
#
# ⚠ ggdef CANNOT ADJUDICATE THIS ONE: `Mutex` is outside the phase-0 subset
# (`unresolved callee `Mutex``), so the truth axis here is C + ASan, and the
# expected value is read off the program's own meaning rather than the oracle's.
# Its `Callable` sibling IS ggdef-adjudicated and prints `41` there.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the `#[ignore]`d
# `known_gap_closure_capture_mutex_block_scope_uaf`): prints `41`, rc 0,
# ASan-clean.

void main():
    Callable[int()] outer = (): 0
    int n = 1
    while n > 0:
        Mutex[int] m = Mutex[int](41)
        outer = (): m.lock().get()
        n = n - 1
    print(outer())
